      "description": "The DMARC policy for caltech.edu is p=none, which asks receivers to take no action on mail that fails authentication. The SPF record also ends in '?all', reported separately as spf-too-permissive. It describes the same exposure from the SPF side: count the two as one.",
      "impact": "Mail forged as this domain is still delivered. p=none is a monitoring posture, useful while you find your legitimate senders, but it stops nothing.",
      "remediation": "Once your rua reports show every legitimate sender passing, change p=none to p=quarantine, then to p=reject. Move in that order and watch the reports at each step.",
      "references": [
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7489#section-6.3"
      ],
