      "description": "DKIM keys below 2048 bits are published at default._domainkey.caltech.edu (1024 bits) and s2._domainkey.caltech.edu (1024 bits). Each meets the RFC 8301 minimum of 1024 bits, below the recommended 2048. The domain also publishes selector1._domainkey.caltech.edu, selector2._domainkey.caltech.edu, k2._domainkey.caltech.edu, s1._domainkey.caltech.edu. We cannot tell from DNS which selector it signs its mail with. RFC 6376 section 6.1.2 has a verifier fetch the key named by the signature's s= tag, so a signature may name any selector the domain publishes, the weaker one included.",
